.TH CADE 1 "April 2026" "C.A.D.E. 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cade \- Community Application Development Environment command-line interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cade
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
C.A.D.E. is a collaborative application development environment.
The \fBcade\fR command initializes environments, creates projects,
and reports module and environment status.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Initialize the C.A.D.E. environment.
.TP
.B create <name>
Create a new project with the supplied name.
.TP
.B list
List available modules.
.TP
.B status
Show environment status.
.TP
.B help
Show command help output.
.TP
.B man
Show a short manual summary and where to find the full man page.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Show help output.
.SH EXAMPLES
.B cade init
.br
.B cade create sci-fi-writer
.br
.B cade status
.SH FILES
.TP
.B man/cade.1
Project man page source.
.TP
.B docs/CLI_HELP.md
Extended command help.
